{
  "id": "03934_tagayasu",
  "headword": "{耕|たがや}す",
  "reading": "たがやす",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to till; to plow; to cultivate",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to till; to plow",
      "explanation": "To prepare soil for planting by turning it over."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to cultivate",
      "explanation": "To work the land for agricultural purposes."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{畑|はたけ}を{耕|たがや}して{野菜|やさい}を{植|う}えた。",
      "english": "I tilled the field and planted vegetables.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{祖父|そふ}は{毎朝|まいあさ}{田|た}んぼを{耕|たがや}している。",
      "english": "My grandfather tills the rice paddy every morning.",
      "notes": "Habitual action",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{土|つち}を{耕|たがや}すのは{重労働|じゅうろうどう}だ。",
      "english": "Tilling soil is hard work.",
      "notes": "Nominalized form with の",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{春|はる}になったら{庭|にわ}を{耕|たがや}して{花|はな}を{植|う}えよう。",
      "english": "When spring comes, let's till the garden and plant flowers.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex5",
      "japanese": "この{土地|とち}は{昔|むかし}から{耕|たがや}されてきた。",
      "english": "This land has been cultivated since long ago.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03934_tagayasu_ex6",
      "japanese": "{機械|きかい}を{使|つか}って{広|ひろ}い{農地|のうち}を{耕|たがや}している。",
      "english": "They cultivate a large farmland using machinery.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{耕|たがや}す is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\nThe ている form indicates ongoing or habitual action ({畑|はたけ}を{耕|たがや}している = 'is tilling the field' or 'tills the field regularly').\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [land]を{耕|たがや}す (till/plow ~)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {畑|はたけ}を{耕|たがや}す (till a field)\n- {田|た}んぼを{耕|たがや}す (plow a rice paddy)\n- {土|つち}を{耕|たがや}す (work the soil)\n\nRelated to the noun {耕作|こうさく} (cultivation) and {農耕|のうこう} (farming).",
